Count the entries into probeCandidates

Every start and load on the panel is closed: IOSurface's start returns and then
nothing.  The last stall inside a kext is ruled out, so the question is whether
the matching loop is spinning or blocked before it.

M<count> every 64 entries, panic at 200000 with the thread's backtrace.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
index 6d7dd7e..7a92126 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
@@ -3778,6 +3778,21 @@ IOService::invokeNotifiers(OSArray * willSend[])
 void
 IOService::probeCandidates( OSOrderedSet * matches )
 {
+	/* nio: the panel now ends on a closed start/load pair -- IOSurface's
+	 * start() returns and nothing follows, with every enter line of its own
+	 * matched by a leave.  That puts the stall between two kexts, in the
+	 * matching machinery.  Count the entries: a panel that keeps printing M<n>
+	 * is a loop that never settles, and one that stops printing is a stall
+	 * before this function; either way the ambiguity is gone. */
+	{
+		static uint32_t nio_probe_cand;
+		if ((++nio_probe_cand & 0x3fu) == 0) {
+			printf("\nM%u", nio_probe_cand);
+		}
+		if (nio_probe_cand >= 200000u) {
+			panic("nio: probeCandidates called %u times", nio_probe_cand);
+		}
+	}
 	OSDictionary        *       match = NULL;
 	OSSymbol            *       symbol;
 	IOService           *       inst;
